7:02:19Z","closed_at":"2026-08-28T17:02:19Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in:\n- 4.7 dev 3\n- 4.6.1 (dotnet build)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Nvidia RTX 3070 - Intel i7 12700f - 16 GB Ram\n\n### Issue description\n\nJolt physics seems to cause a lot of lag when having a lot of overlapping Area3Ds. GodotPhysics does not seem to lag during just overlap. Jiggling the bodies in GodotPhysics a small amount still does not cause lag, however, jiggling them a larger amount will start to lag. I assume that the cause of that is that during no/low jiggle, areas aren't triggering enter/exits. Jolt however, will lag with no/low jiggle. Someone seems to have made a comment on another slightly different Jolt Area3D issue here https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106482#issuecomment-3067074705 depicting something more similar to here.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nStep 1: Create a lot of Areas\nStep 2: Make sure they are all monitoring and monitorable\n\nIn the test project, on the Node3D labeled \"Areas\", setting the jiggle value to low numbers, like 0.0 or 0.1, will not cause lag during overlaps in GodotPhysics, but will in JoltPhysics. There seems to be lag from areas first entering in GodotPhysics, but remains stable if areas don't leave eachother. Setting it to a higher value like 1.0 will start to cause lag in GodotPhysics, (assumedly) from entering and exiting. Jolt Physics still seems a bit slower than GodotPhysics when Jiggle is set to 1.0.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[area-3d-overlap-lag.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26387734/area-3d-overlap-lag.zip)\nOpen Scene.tscn\nSelect the Node3D labelled \"areas\".\nThe Jiggle strength value shifts the areas by that amount multiplied by a random vector3. Low values do not cause lag in GodotPhysics, but do in Jolt Physics. High values cause lag in both.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118047/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118047/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}